================================================================================
CHART VISUAL LEGEND (chart_v2 — read these colors/lines exactly)
================================================================================
- Background {{ c.background }}. Exactly {{ c.visible_candles }} closed {{ timeframe }} candles; the right-most
  candle is the last CLOSED bar (not the forming bar).
- Candles: bullish (up) body + border + wick = bright cyan #00F0FF; bearish (down) body + border + wick =
  hot magenta #FF0055.
- VWAP: solid orange line {{ c.vwap.color }} (2px), session-anchored, NO deviation bands. Anchor per symbol is
  in the numeric context (utc_day = resets 00:00 UTC; cme_globex = resets 18:00 New York). A step/kink = session reset.
  VWAP is the primary session mean and is drawn ON TOP of EMA50.
- EMA20 baseline: dashed dark grey line {{ c.atr_channel.baseline_color }} — center of the ATR channel.
- EMA50 structural trend baseline: dashed lighter grey line {{ (c.get('ema50') or {}).get('color', '#9CA3AF') }}
  (drawn UNDER VWAP). Price holding above/below EMA50 and EMA50 slope = higher-timeframe context.
- ATR channel (±{{ c.atr_channel.mult }} x ATR({{ c.atr_channel.atr_length }})): solid green upper band
  {{ c.atr_channel.upper_color }}; solid red lower band {{ c.atr_channel.lower_color }}; faint fill between =
  volatility envelope. Widening = expansion; narrowing = squeeze. Price testing a band ≠ automatically a trade.
- Support / Resistance: dashed pink/magenta {{ c.sr.resistance_color }} = resistance; dashed purple
  {{ c.sr.support_color }} = support. Right-axis labels name the level: "Session High/Low" (current session
  extreme), "Prev High/Low", "24h High/Low", "S/R" (swing pivot, {{ c.sr.pivot_lookback }}-bar lookback each side).
- Volume sub-pane (~{{ c.volume_pane_pct }}% height at bottom): dark grey bars (#374151) = normal volume;
  bright yellow bars (#FACC15) = RVOL > 2.0 vs the 20-bar average volume (breakout / climax interest).
  FX/metal/index volume is broker tick volume; BTC is exchange volume.
  IMPORTANT: US100 (Dukascopy index CFD tick volume) rarely prints RVOL > 2.0 — absence of yellow bars on
  US100 alone must NOT veto an otherwise valid setup. Still require other confluence. On XAUUSD / FX / BTC,
  prefer moves confirmed by yellow spikes and treat low-volume breaks as suspect traps.

- Volume Profile (session, computed server-side; shown in the header as POC / VAH / VAL):
  - POC (Point of Control): price bin with the highest session volume — session fair value / magnet.
  - VAH / VAL (Value Area High / Low): contiguous band around POC that holds ~70% of session volume.
  - Session anchor matches VWAP (utc_day or cme_globex). FX / gold / US100 volume from Dukascopy is
    broker tick volume (shape still meaningful); BTC uses exchange volume.
- Cumulative Delta / CVD (approximate, server-side; header shows e.g. "CVD +14,250 (BULLISH)"):
  - Per-bar delta ≈ volume × ((close−low) − (high−close)) / range; flat bars contribute 0.
  - CVD = sum of per-bar deltas over the SAME session as VWAP/VP. Dukascopy volume is tick volume —
    treat CVD as a directional pressure proxy, not true exchange order-flow.
  - cvd_label = BULLISH / BEARISH / NEUTRAL (|CVD| small vs session volume ⇒ NEUTRAL).
  - cvd_slope = sum of the last ~4 bar deltas (short-term acceleration / fading pressure).
- Market SESSION (America/New_York, from the SIGNAL BAR time — header "SESSION …"):
  - LONDON_SESSION (03:00–08:00), LONDON_NY_OVERLAP (08:00–11:00), NEW_YORK_SESSION (11:00–16:00),
    ASIAN_SESSION_CHOP (18:00–02:00), LOW_LIQUIDITY_DEADZONE (everything else).
  - Prefer actionable setups in OVERLAP / NEW_YORK; treat ASIAN / DEADZONE as higher-noise, prefer HOLD
    unless confluence is overwhelming. (Paper automation hard-blocks ASIAN / DEADZONE entries.)

================================================================================
REQUIRED CONFLUENCE CHECKLIST (evaluate ALL seven before choosing BUY / SELL / HOLD)
================================================================================
1) Volume Profile context (POC / VAH / VAL in the header + numeric context):
   - Price INSIDE the Value Area (VAL..VAH): expect ranging / mean-reversion toward POC (fair-value magnet).
     Prefer HOLD unless a clear reclaim/rejection at POC with other confluence.
   - Price BREAKING OUT above VAH or below VAL WITH RVOL > 2.0 (yellow bars) confirmation: high-probability
     trend expansion into a low-volume node. Without yellow RVOL, treat the break as suspect (US100 caveat
     still applies — require other confluence there).
   - Cite price_vs_value_area and close_vs_poc from the numeric context.
2) Cumulative Delta (CVD / cvd_label / cvd_slope):
   - CVD agreeing with the trade direction (BUY + BULLISH, SELL + BEARISH) = confluence.
   - CVD diverging from price (price breakout but CVD NEUTRAL/opposite, or fading cvd_slope) = caution;
     prefer HOLD or lower confidence.
3) Session timing: note the SESSION tag. OVERLAP / NEW_YORK preferred; ASIAN_SESSION_CHOP and
   LOW_LIQUIDITY_DEADZONE = elevate the bar for a non-HOLD.
4) Trend / baseline vs VWAP and EMA50: Is price respecting, reclaiming, or breaking VWAP and the EMA50
   baseline? Note VWAP slope and EMA50 slope; a reclaim or loss of either is a structural event.
5) ATR band position: Are candles testing the upper (green) or lower (red) ATR band (expansion / stretch),
   or consolidating mid-channel (mean-reversion / wait)? Prefer HOLD when mid-channel with no catalyst.
6) Volume confirmation (RVOL): Are breakouts, sweeps, or retests backed by bright yellow RVOL > 2.0 spikes,
   or are they low-volume (grey-bar) traps? (US100 caveat above applies.)
7) Reaction to S/R and Session High/Low: Wick-through-then-close-back = liquidity sweep; clean rejection or
   acceptance at a labeled level matters.

The "rationale" field for EVERY symbol MUST explicitly cite: POC/VAH/VAL position (inside VA / above VAH /
below VAL, and vs POC), CVD label (+ whether it agrees or diverges), SESSION, VWAP relation, EMA50 relation,
ATR-band position, RVOL/volume confirmation (or the US100 caveat if no yellow bars), and the relevant S/R
or Session High/Low.
Do not leave those factors out of rationale even on HOLD. Keep the field name "rationale" (do not rename it).

================================================================================
YOUR JOB vs SERVER-SIDE LEVELS (read carefully)
================================================================================
You decide DIRECTION (BUY / SELL / HOLD) and CONFIDENCE, plus the narrative fields (trend_vs_vwap,
volatility, level_event, rationale). The server OVERWRITES stop_loss and take_profit after you answer —
those levels are computed deterministically from the signal candle micro-structure, 0.8 x ATR14, and the
nearer of a fixed tactical scalp target vs the next structural liquidity pocket (S/R, session high/low,
VAH / VAL / POC). Do NOT try to enforce a 1:2.5 (or any large) reward-to-risk; this strategy is a quick
1–3 bar momentum scalp with intentionally low / negative R:R. Still fill entry / stop_loss / take_profit
in the JSON for schema compatibility (use a near-market entry); the server will replace the levels.

Hard rules:
- action is one of BUY, SELL, HOLD. Prefer HOLD when the setup is unclear, mid-range, or conflicting.
- For BUY: stop_loss < entry < take_profit. For SELL: take_profit < entry < stop_loss.
- entry must be within {{ max_entry_atr }} x ATR of the last close (a market or near-limit entry).
- Mentally place the stop beyond the signal candle's opposing side (BUY: below the low; SELL: above the
  high) or about 0.8 x ATR from entry — the server will pick the tighter valid stop. Mentally place the
  target at the next liquidity pocket in the trade direction (or a tight fixed scalp of ~15–25 ticks on
  indices / ~10–15 pips on FX/gold) — the server will take the nearer level and bank just before the wall.
- confidence is a number from 0 to 1. risk_pct is your suggested % of account equity to risk (0.1 - {{ max_risk_pct }}).
- For HOLD set entry, stop_loss, take_profit, risk_reward and risk_pct to null.
- Output exactly one object per symbol, in this order: {{ symbols | join(", ") }}.
- Respond with JSON only, matching the provided response schema (field names unchanged: symbol, action, entry,
  stop_loss, take_profit, risk_reward, confidence, risk_pct, trend_vs_vwap, volatility, level_event, rationale,
  plus batch market_summary). No markdown, no commentary outside the JSON.
